    "## Defining the Sentinel-2 Study Area and Spatial Reference\n",
    "\n",
    "To maintain consistency with earlier Landsat feature engineering, the same combined bounding box was reused to define the Sentinel-2 study area, ensuring both sensors operate over an identical geographic extent covering Manhattan and the Bronx. This alignment is essential for reliable multi-sensor fusion and prevents spatial inconsistencies between thermal and spectral features.\n",
    "\n",
    "The bounding box was first represented in WGS84 for compatibility with satellite indexing, then reprojected into **UTM Zone 18N**, the appropriate metric coordinate system for New York City. This projection ensures that all subsequent spatial operations—such as buffering, aggregation, and pixel-to-building alignment—are performed in real-world units.\n",
    "\n",
    "This step establishes a shared, projection-safe spatial foundation for Sentinel-2 extraction, allowing reflectance and red-edge features to be integrated without introducing coordinate or scale-related artifacts."
   ]
