    "## Selecting Optimal Sentinel Scenes\n",
    "With the study area and spatial reference fixed, the next step identifies the most suitable Sentinel scenes for feature extraction. Rather than relying on a single acquisition by assumption, the pipeline searches across multiple candidate scenes spanning the summer season to ensure robustness against cloud contamination and acquisition gaps.\n",
    "\n",
    "For Sentinel-2, scenes were queried over the defined study area within a June–September window, with an explicit cloud cover threshold applied. From the available candidates, the scene closest in time to **July 24, 2021**—the date of the ground and Landsat observations—was selected. This minimizes temporal mismatch while preserving data quality.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same temporal search strategy was applied to Sentinel-1, ensuring radar-based context is aligned in space and time with optical features. Although cloud filtering is not required for Sentinel-1, selecting the closest acquisition date maintains consistency across sensors.\n",
    "\n",
    "This step ensures that downstream feature extraction is grounded in scenes that are spatially overlapping, temporally aligned, and quality-controlled—establishing a reliable observational basis before any spectral, textural, or neighborhood-level Sentinel features are derived."
