    "All building geometries are first standardized to WGS84 to ensure consistent coordinate handling, after which a unique `building_key` is constructed from centroid latitude and longitude when not already present. This key provides a reproducible identifier for linking Sentinel-derived features back to the tabular UHI dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "The centroids are then reprojected into **UTM Zone 18N**, placing all downstream spatial operations into a metric coordinate system. This ensures that pixel offsets, buffers, and distance-based aggregation around each building reflect real-world spatial scales.\n",
    "\n",
    "This step establishes a clean, projection-safe set of building centroids, forming the spatial backbone for consistent, building-aligned Sentinel feature extraction in the subsequent stages of the pipeline."
