    "## Extracting Building-Scale Sentinel-2 Features\n",
    "With building centroids prepared, the pipeline proceeds to extract Sentinel-2 features that capture vegetation condition, surface moisture, and built-material characteristics around each structure. Rather than using raw pixel values, features are summarized within **200 m buffers** around building centroids, aligning with the spatial scale used in earlier clustering and UHI diagnostics.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key Sentinel-2 spectral bands (visible, red-edge, NIR, and SWIR) are loaded and spatially clipped to the study area. All reflectance values are scaled to physical units, and bands with coarser resolution are resampled to ensure consistency before index computation. This guarantees that derived features are spatially comparable and free from resolution-induced artifacts.\n",
    "\n",
    "From these bands, a targeted set of indices is computed:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Vegetation and moisture signals** (e.g., NDVI, NDMI) to capture cooling capacity and plant stress\n",
    "* **Red-edge–based metrics** (e.g., REPI) to detect subtle vegetation stress not visible in standard indices\n",
    "* **Built-surface indicators** (e.g., built fraction, material property indices) to characterize heat-retaining urban fabric\n",
    "\n",
    "For each building buffer, zonal statistics are computed to summarize the mean, variability, and valid pixel coverage of each index. Processing is performed in batches to maintain memory stability while scaling across thousands of structures.\n",
    "\n",
    "This step translates raw Sentinel-2 imagery into physically meaningful, building-aligned features—bridging spectral information with the urban form and setting the stage for seamless integration into the final UHI modeling dataset."
   ]
